  "configuration_id": "config_034",
  "reason": "The best result so far is config_009 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + avgpool + weighted, acc=0.6776, 5.90 GPU hrs). The key evidence is: (1) scvi_n200 substantially outperforms pca_n2000 (~4% gain), (2) avgpool beats transformer aggregation, and (3) weighted fusion beats concat. The main remaining uncertainty is whether imagenet_vit_l can match or exceed resnet50 as the image encoder in the scvi_n200 context. With pca_n2000, the two image encoders were nearly tied (0.6390 vs 0.6352), and imagenet_vit_l was cheaper (7.02 vs 10.60 GPU hrs). config_034 tests this exact swap while keeping all other settings at their proven-best values. If it matches or beats config_009, we get a cheaper top configuration; if it falls short, we confirm resnet50 is optimal and can direct the remaining 2 experiments toward other levers (e.g., singleprofile or scgpt). Expected relative cost: moderate, roughly 6–8 GPU hours (comparable to config_026's 7.02 hrs, since it uses imagenet_vit_l with avgpool+weighted fusion, avoiding the expensive concat pathway)."
}

